From 5d139d153587908026987021883993480f2350dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 04:11:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: extend BRF kcov wrap to add_addr_hmac_valid

Patch 0002 wrapped three subflow-level validity gates
(subflow_token_join_request, subflow_hmac_valid, subflow_thmac_valid)
with the BRF kcov remote macros so coverage from the MP_JOIN
authentication path is attributed to the per-msk kcov handle plumbed
via MPTCP_KCOV_HANDLE.  Patch 0004 extended the wrap to the option
parser entry (mptcp_get_options / mptcp_parse_option).

This patch closes a remaining coverage blind spot: the ADD_ADDR
HMAC validation function.  The BRF harness already mutates ADD_ADDR
HMAC bytes via the NFQUEUE wire-mutation worker (gap 7,
MPTCP_PM_OPT_ADDR_HMAC), but without a kcov wrap on
add_addr_hmac_valid the coverage-guided corpus is blind to whether
those mutations actually reach the validator's body or are rejected
earlier on the parse path.  Adding the wrap completes the loop
between the harness's mutation surface and the corpus's coverage
feedback.

Structurally identical to patch 0002's wraps: snapshot the kcov
handle once via BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START(msk), start AFTER the cheap
echo bypass (that early return is uninteresting and not worth
instrumenting), stop before return.  Runs in softirq context
(option parser path), which patch 0005's in_serving_softirq()
guard already covers.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-7
Signed-off-by: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
---
 net/mptcp/options.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/options.c b/net/mptcp/options.c
index 58cba581f7907..d27b42d74aee2 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/options.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/options.c
@@ -1144,10 +1144,12 @@ static bool add_addr_hmac_valid(struct mptcp_sock *msk,
 				struct mptcp_options_received *mp_opt)
 {
 	u64 hmac = 0;
+	bool ok;
 
 	if (mp_opt->echo)
 		return true;
 
+	BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START(msk);
 	hmac = add_addr_generate_hmac(READ_ONCE(msk->remote_key),
 				      READ_ONCE(msk->local_key),
 				      &mp_opt->addr);
@@ -1155,7 +1157,9 @@ static bool add_addr_hmac_valid(struct mptcp_sock *msk,
 	pr_debug("msk=%p, ahmac=%llu, mp_opt->ahmac=%llu\n",
 		 msk, hmac, mp_opt->ahmac);
 
-	return hmac == mp_opt->ahmac;
+	ok = hmac == mp_opt->ahmac;
+	BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_STOP(msk);
+	return ok;
 }
 
 /* Return false in case of error (or subflow has been reset),
